in  protagonists are quite difficult  especially with what's being set up in  judas kaisen and there's even been some  evidence to suggest that akutami didn't  put an extensive amount of thought into  yuji when creating him as when asked  about his previous renown as the tiger  of west junior high akutami admitted  that they didn't consider why that  epithet was given but in the end yuji is  the primary anchor of the series and as  an author i imagine that's why akutami  is so hyper focused and harsh on  themselves when it comes to yuji  specifically although i should say that  i for one think he's pretty damn  compelling this does take us to yuji fun  fact number the second however and anime  watches may be somewhat shocked to learn  this but yuji was not the original  protagonist of jujutsu kaiser in fact in  a rather trippy sentence jujitsukai sen  itself is not even the original jujutsu  kaisen the series itself actually began  as a four chapter mini manga which was  helmed by protagonist yuta okotsu and  uta and yuji while they're very similar  in many many ways specifically  narratively because they both commence  the series scheduled to be executed and  there's a lot of similarities so this  may even explain some of our kotami's  trouble with yuji because yuta had a  very compelling story which will be  explored in the upcoming jujutsu kaisen  film and when starting the sequel series  yuji was created to fill that uta role  just with a bunch of different  circumstances and because yuta does  exist in jiu jitsu kaisen akatami  obviously couldn't just copy and paste  too much of yoota onto yuji so it does  lead to a potentially awkward situation  where we need to hit those same story  and character beats just in a slightly  different way and all of which is to say  that if you have not checked out the  jiu-jitsu kaisen prequel then absolutely  go and do it or i guess wait for the  film it's coming out soon enough either  way it's fascinating insight into what  