 actress and ever since  then eugene has been something of a big  fan of her to say the least although the  designation of his type has led to a  fair bit of fun in the jujitsu kaisen  fanbase and in fact yuji's english  dubbed voice actor even comedically  redid the famous line but substituting  in megan the stallion thus leading to  many a megan meme but while his  preference in women may be very very  clear yuji's taste in food is anything  but his favorite food has been  identified as quote unquote rice bowl  with food on top so food with more food  and his least favorite food has been  registered as none so this man will  quite literally eat anything i suppose  which you know it actually makes a lot  of sense hence why he is so eager to  devour all of those tasty tasty sukuna  fingies it is a bit unusual for a shonen  protagonist though because even the big  trophy eaters usually have something  that puts them off like for luffy that's  cherry pie finato that's fresh  vegetables but for yuji nothing is off  the table which means that he really  does put the eat in itadore oh and also  it leads nicely into our next fun fact  because gege akitami was posed the  question of what would happen if fuji  consumed one of the death paintings  which just as a tldr recap they are  cursed whom existences that can evolve  into half human half ghost spirits when  implanted into a human vessel however  that idea becomes a bit tricky when it  comes to yuji because he already shares  his fleshy vessel with the king of  curses ryo min sukuna so while this is  definitely a more academic exercise the  question of what would happen if fuji  consumed to death painting does still  exist especially considering how eager  he seems to be to consume anything and  everything and according to akhitami  should this event occur then the death  painting existence would simply be  destroyed by sukuna however another  scenario was given to us as well which  is what would happen if uga to death  painting prior to consuming sukina's  finger and this is very interesting  because apparently the death painting  would not be able to evolve itself into  a hybrid with yuji's body and instead it  would be consumed and yuji would inherit  its cursed energy so either way it's  pretty bad outcome for the hypothetical  painting in question although it does  further reinforce yuju's absurd ability  to curses and according to fun fact  number seven yuji may also have some  other useful natural resistances because  apparently his body fat percentage is  within single digit numbers now this is  particularly intriguing because the  average male body fat percentage would  be between 18 to 24 and we don't even  reach the single digit numbers until we  hit the realm of athletes who average  between six to 13 so yuji's general  fitness is certainly on par with the  greatest of physical specimens that this  world has to offer despite the fact that  he will as established eat pretty much  anything it's quite envious really  because yuji doesn't seem to pay too  much attention to any kind of dieting he  just eats what he wants in reasonable  portions i suppose and is granted the  form of an adonis as a reward for his  doing nothing however there may also be  a logical in-world explanation for this  due to the concept of heavenly  restrictions previous restriction users  that we've seen such as maki and  tojizenin have had documented cases of  physical strength being heavily buffed  in exchange for less or even no control  of cursed energy and yuji could be in a  very similar situation because right now  i see no other explanation for his  insane abilities but particularly his  power to maintain single-digit body fat  with his uh whatever his lifestyle is  but as part of this lifestyle yuji has  also been documented as being the best  cook amongst the first year to do to  students although i'm not quite sure how  much that means because there's only  three of them and the other two happen  to be megami fushiguru and  noborakugisaki two characters who i  would never think to award praise in the  culinary field but i suppose it does  make sense yuji does have the shonen  protagonist syndrome whereby his parents  were never around and even though he was  raised by his grandfather that would  quickly have turned into eugene needing  to learn quite a few basics about life  just in order to help out which of  course includes cooking and just in case  you were curious when it comes to the  second best cook amongst the first year  students akutami claims that it's a bit  of a sad tie neither fushiguru nor  kugisaki have any skill relevant enough  to be separated from one another so  all hail yuji i guess and speaking of  hailing yuji we should all take a moment  to recognize that he is currently one of  the dual world record holders for the  most consecutive number of black flash  attacks performed which is pretty  astounding for someone who had only been  using cursed energy for what a handful  of months before performing this feat  still the explanation for that is pretty  simple according to fellow world record  holder ken to anonymity who states that  after the first black flash the  performer enters the zone and thus  making subsequent black flashes  theoretically easier to produce rather  than pulling one out of nowhere like the  initial instance but today yugi and  nanami have performed the technique four  times in a row each and this record does  get a little bit confusing because a lot  of fans forget that it was talking about  performing the attack consecutively  which yuji did four times against hanami  however he did also perform a fifth or i  guess first black flash earlier on in  the fight which often leads people to  believe that he actually broke the  record sadly however that first black  flash is invalid because there were many  many other attacks that came in between  that and the consecutive four but still  yuji the dude performed five black  flashes in a single day and that feels  pretty damn impressive but quite  possibly the most intriguing and also  kind of concerning fact about yuji is  that gege akutami still has not decided  what his ultimate fate will be at this  point in the judicial manga we are  stated to be about halfway through and  that akutami has quite a clear road map  to the end of the series for example  characters like fushiguro have their  story set in stone but that is not the  case for yuji and this may once again  have to do with the difficulties akitami  has with writing the character but i  find it quite interesting that there is  a legitimate question mark as to his  ultimate fate because in my mind there  are only two basic options one being  that yuji lives and the other being that  yuji dies and i don't want to make  myself sound too bloodthirsty here but i  am very much in the camp of the latter i  very much liked the idea that jujutsu  kaisen was set up to arrive at the  inevitable conclusion of yuji's death  whether that be via execution  sacrificing himself to reward asukana or  even potentially another way it doesn't  matter so long as it satisfies his  grandfather's last words of making sure  not to die alone and i think that a  series like jujutsu kaisen could  actually pull off killing its  protagonist in a way that many many  others could not akutami has never been  shy of exploring dark not even dark but  just like somber and depressing ideas in  the series stuff that really hits you in  the emotional testicles and at this  point i feel like yuji living and having  a happy ending would kind of betray  everything that we've been working up  towards until now however with that said  i am not a world class manga author i am  a random australian dude guy and i very  much trust akutami's intuition when it  comes to storytelling thinking about it  i have very few criticisms of jujutsukai  sin in that regard it's almost  unbelievable really because i tend to  rip other series apart like brittle  paper but kaisen is it's just really  solid so if akatami has an ending in  mind where yuji does live then yeah  maybe that's the right way to go i just  can't quite see it myself at the moment  and i guess to be fair even akatami  themselves is struggling with landing on  that final choice so for an easy choice  to make here's another video to watch i  promise it'll be great fun just like  this one so i look forward to seeing you  there

